# pnpm configuration for the BOSC workspace (Epic #1549, Phase 0 #1550).
#
# We keep pnpm's default isolated (symlinked, non-hoisted) node_modules — that strict
# layout is what retires the npm version foot-guns, so we do NOT `shamefully-hoist`.
#
# The entries below are the minimal, audited escape hatch: a handful of transitive
# ("phantom") dependencies that web/ source imports directly but does not declare. npm's
# flat node_modules made them resolvable by accident; pnpm's strict layout surfaces them.
# We expose the *exact same* resolved instances (not new declared versions) via
# public-hoist so the dependency graph — and the built dist/ — stay byte-identical to the
# npm build. Declaring them as first-class deps would risk a second copy of luma.gl / vite
# diverging from what deck.gl / astro resolve, and duplicate luma.gl instances break
# deck.gl's runtime class-identity checks. The package-split phases (#1551–#1555) will give
# each extracted package a proper, scoped dependency list; until then these are hoisted.
#
#   vite          — plugins/watermark-bundle.ts (a Vite plugin), via astro
#   @luma.gl/*    — components/islands/{Field,Flow}Layer.ts, via @deck.gl
#   unified,
#   remark-parse,
#   remark-mdx,
#   vfile         — src/lib/storyCompile.ts, via @astrojs/mdx
#   @types/hast,
#   @types/unist  — type-only imports in rehype-doc-links.ts / storyCompile.ts
public-hoist-pattern[]=vite
public-hoist-pattern[]=@luma.gl/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=unified
public-hoist-pattern[]=remark-parse
public-hoist-pattern[]=remark-mdx
public-hoist-pattern[]=vfile
public-hoist-pattern[]=@types/hast
public-hoist-pattern[]=@types/unist
